    <http://example.org/node/chunk63> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Additionally, our context notes that the sovereign HDS tier and Sovereign European Model are more cost-efficient on the recurring side than the premium high-availability tier combined with top-tier proprietary inference. This information could be used to propose a cost-efficient solution that meets the client's requirements while optimizing costs." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message12> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk64> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "However, specific details about how cost-optimization strategies to meet the budget constraints of 900,000 over 5 years apply to this particular contract or how cost-optimization strategies to meet the budget constraints of 900,000 over 5 years can be implemented within the given budget are not provided in our company context. Therefore, I do not have enough information to provide a detailed plan for cost optimization on this project." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message12> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk65> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution must provide intelligent assistance tools, support clinical-administrative activities, facilitate access to information, improve quality of written outputs, reduce processing and documentation times, and ensure continuity of care between professionals and services. The solution must also be explainable, with recommendations or suggestions produced being grounded in source data and auditable a posteriori." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message14> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk66> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "How will our AI innovation strategy meet these requirements, and what trade-offs will our need to make to balance the level of automation with the need for human oversight and validation? our AI innovation strategy is centered around leveraging retrieval-augmented generation capabilities to provide intelligent assistance tools that support clinical-administrative activities. our AI innovation strategy grounds answers in Faber IA own validated documents, ensuring that recommendations or suggestions are explainable and auditable a posteriori. grounds aligns with requirements for explainability and continuity of care. To facilitate access to information and improve the quality of written outputs, our AI innovation strategy utilizes hybrid retrieval, re-ranking, query reformulation, and multi-document synthesis capabilities. hybrid retrieval, re-ranking, query reformulation, and multi-document synthesis capabilities enable staff to efficiently access reliable, up-to-date information drawn from internal procedures, care protocols, and applicable regulations, thus improving the quality of written outputs." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message14> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk67> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Regarding the reduction of processing and documentation times, our template-guided drafting and structured extraction capabilities (such as assisting with PMSI/ICD-10 coding) can significantly streamline clinical and administrative tasks. By integrating into existing workflows without introducing a rupture, our ensure that our AI innovation strategy fits into the staff's current practices, thereby reducing the learning curve and increasing efficiency." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message14> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk68> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To balance the level of automation with the need for human oversight and validation, our AI innovation strategy incorporates human validation into the workflow. The assistant proposes, but the professional validates, ensuring that clinical or medico-administrative decisions are not automated without explicit validation by a qualified professional." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message14> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk69> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "This approach maintains the integrity of decision-making processes while leveraging AI to reduce workload and improve consistency. Trade-offs may involve selecting between different model options - such as our sovereign European open-weight model, which offers full auditability and strong grounding behavior but may have somewhat lower raw performance on complex generative tasks, versus top-tier proprietary models that offer higher performance but less internal transparency." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message14> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk7> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "As an indication, a response time below 2 seconds is expected for common queries. A high level of answer relevance is expected. 5.2 Availability. Continuity of care requires a high level of availability, including outside office hours (24/7 services). An availability target of the order of 99.9% is expected. 5.3 Integration and interoperability. The solution must integrate with the existing hospital information system (SIH) and the electronic patient record (DPI)." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk70> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The choice will be made per engagement, trading off performance against explainability and sovereignty. Ultimately, by carefully designing the interaction between AI-driven tools and human professionals, our can ensure that our AI innovation strategy not only meets the technical requirements but also respects the ethical and regulatory constraints of the healthcare sector, providing a balanced approach to automation and human oversight." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message14> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk71> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client wishes to limit the environmental footprint of The client information systems. The titleholder must propose a solution that contributes to reducing energy consumption and relies, as far as possible, on low-carbon infrastructure." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk72> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "How will our CSR sustainability strategy ensure these requirements are met, and what benefits can our expect from implementing sustainable practices in this project? Our company, Faber IA, has a strong commitment to sustainability, which is reflected in Our company, Faber IA CSR profile." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk73> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Our company, Faber IA have published a trajectory to reduce carbon intensity per managed assistant year on year, demonstrating Our company, Faber IA dedication to minimizing our environmental impact. In terms of infrastructure, Our company, Faber IA partner with green hosting providers like OuraneCloud, which offers sovereign hosting in the EU, renewable energy, and a power usage effectiveness (PUE) of 1.2, indicating efficient energy use." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk74> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Additionally, Our company, Faber IA reuse heat, further reducing waste and environmental footprint. To reduce energy consumption, Our company, Faber IA implement digital sobriety practices such as model right-sizing, caching, and batching. digital sobriety practices such as model right-sizing, caching, and batching not only decrease the energy required to operate Our company, Faber IA solutions but also contribute to a more efficient use of resources." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk75> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "By choosing Our company, Faber IA, the client can benefit from Our company, Faber IA expertise in sustainable IT practices, which will help reduce the environmental footprint of the client information systems. Our company, Faber IA solution will rely on low-carbon infrastructure and contribute to reducing energy consumption, aligning with The titleholder requirements and supporting a more environmentally friendly project outcome." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk76> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Moreover, Our company, Faber IA carbon reporting capability ensures transparency regarding the carbon footprint of Our company, Faber IA operations, allowing for informed decisions and continuous improvement in sustainability performance. This commitment to sustainability not only benefits the environment but also enhances Our company, Faber IA reputation and relationships with clients who prioritize environmental responsibility." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk77> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Our company, Faber IA, proposes an artificial intelligence solution designed to assist hospital staff in hospital staff daily activities at Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB). Our company, Faber IA approach, grounded in retrieval-augmented generation capabilities, provides an intelligent assistance tool accessible from hospital staff work environment. an intelligent assistance tool accessible from the hospital staff's work environment supports clinical-administrative activities by facilitating access to reliable, up-to-date information drawn from internal procedures, care protocols, and applicable regulations. Our company, Faber IA solution, Atelier, is built on a hybrid delivery model that combines agile iterations with a phase-gate structure suited to public and health procurement." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message17> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk78> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Our company, Faber IA break down the project into distinct phases: Framing, Design, Pilot, Generalisation, and Run. Each phase ends with a formal review and a go/no-go decision, ensuring Our company, Faber IA meet the client's requirements and expectations before proceeding to the next phase. Our company, Faber IA integrates with the existing hospital information system (SIH) and electronic patient record (DPI), supporting health interoperability standards such as HL7/FHIR." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message17> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk79> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Our company, Faber IA API-first design provides REST and webhook APIs that are well-documented, allowing for seamless integration into existing work environments, including user directories such as LDAP and Entra ID, through SSO protocols like SAML and OIDC. To ensure data sovereignty, Our company, Faber IA hosting options include the Sovereign HDS tier on OuraneCloud, which is SecNumCloud-qualified, HDS-certified, and located within the EU. the Sovereign HDS tier on OuraneCloud, which is SecNumCloud-qualified, HDS-certified, and located within the EU also supports the requirement for renewable-powered infrastructure, contributing to reduced environmental footprint. Our company, Faber IA implement digital sobriety practices such as model right-sizing, caching, and batching to reduce energy consumption." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message17> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk8> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution must support health interoperability standards (HL7 / FHIR), the national health identifier (INS), and the national framework (Ségur du numérique en santé, Mon espace santé / DMP). API-type interfaces are expected, as is integration with user directories. 6. Sovereignty constraints the authority's attaches particular importance to data sovereignty. Hosting must be performed on SecNumCloud-qualified infrastructure or equivalent, and particular attention will be paid to dependency on non-European suppliers. 7. Budget constraints The global budget allocated to the project is estimated at 900,000 over 5 years." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk80> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Our company, Faber IA solution provides a median latency of 1.3 seconds for common queries, with 95% of common single-document queries below 2 seconds. Our company, Faber IA assists the drafting of clinical and administrative content, including discharge summaries, medical reports, and patient letters, ensuring generated content is adapted to the clinical/administrative context and conforms to expected quality standards. Our company, Faber IA support medical coding (PMSI/ICD-10) for activity reporting (T2A) and take the dossier context into account where available." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message17> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk81> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Our solution facilitates the continuity of care between professionals and services by enabling relevant information sharing, understanding of the context of an in-progress patient pathway, and efficient resumption of handling by another professional. Our company, Faber IA has a strong security and compliance posture, with ISO 27001 and ISO 27701 certifications. Our company, Faber IA guarantee strict compliance with GDPR and ensure health data is treated as special-category data in accordance with GDPR Art. 9." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message17> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk82> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Our company, Faber IA infrastructure holds the French Hébergeur de Données de Santé (HDS) certification, ensuring that Our company, Faber IA processing on Our infrastructure is covered and compliant with the necessary health data hosting regulations. Our company, Faber IA preserve medical confidentiality through encryption at rest (AES-256) and in transit (TLS 1.3), pseudonymisation, and strict access controls via Role-Based Access Control (RBAC). Our solution provides explainability of recommendations or suggestions produced, with a clear audit trail and explanations for Our solution outputs, allowing qualified professionals to validate decisions and maintain medical responsibility." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message17> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk83> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Our solution is designed to fit into the existing practices of staff and does not introduce a rupture in clinical or administrative workflows. Our company, Faber IA provide change management support and training resources to facilitate a smooth transition and adoption of Our solution. Our company, Faber IA target gross margin percentage range is between 25% and 35%, and Our company, Faber IA propose a cost-efficient solution using the sovereign HDS tier and the sovereign European model, which are more cost-efficient on the recurring side." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message17> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk84> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The global budget allocated to the project is estimated at €900,000 over 5 years, with an annual operating cost that remains controlled and compatible with the authority's budgetary capacity. Our company, Faber IA ensure that Our solution contributes to reducing energy consumption and relies as far as possible on low-carbon infrastructure, aligning with Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) sustainable development policy. Our company, Faber IA approach balances the level of automation with the need for human oversight and validation, ensuring that clinical or medico-administrative decisions are not automated without explicit validation by a qualified professional." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message17> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk85> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Our company, Faber IA incorporate human validation into the workflow, maintaining the integrity of decision-making processes while leveraging AI to reduce workload and improve consistency. Ultimately, Our solution is designed to provide a balanced approach to automation and human oversight, respecting ethical and regulatory constraints in the healthcare sector. Our company, Faber IA believe that Our solution meets the requirements and constraints outlined in the call for tenders, providing an intelligent assistance tool that improves the efficiency, quality, and safety of care delivered to patients at Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB)." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message17> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk9> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The annual operating cost must remain controlled and compatible with the authority's budgetary capacity. The titleholder must propose an approach that optimises costs while guaranteeing the expected quality of service. 8. Environmental constraints As part of the authority's sustainable-development policy, the authority's wishes to limit the environmental footprint of the authority's information systems. The titleholder must propose a solution that contributes to reducing energy consumption and relies, as far as possible, on low-carbon infrastructure. 9. Deployment terms the project must be conducted progressively, with a pilot phase on a limited perimeter (one or two departments) followed by progressive generalisation to all services." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

